From 8c1b527dd072b6259922ef144fd8704d19b807df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:41:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): forward providerID and token usage from step events
 to V1 message.updated

The v2 bridge turned session.step.started/ended into message.updated with only
{id, sessionID, role, finish}. V1 consumers read providerID/modelID/tokens from
that event, so the preemptive-compaction token cache never filled on v2: the
hook was structurally inert since the v2 migration (0 [preemptive-compaction]
lines in %TEMP%/oh-my-opencode.log; 15 real fires on Oct 6-9 on v1, none after).

session.step.ended carries the step's tokens (input/output/reasoning/cache) and
session.step.started carries the model ref ({id, providerID, variant}) and the
agent. A stateful shaper (createV1EventShaper) now remembers the model per
assistant message between the two events and joins both into the message.updated
info; the stateless toV1Event still forwards the tokens the ended event itself
carries. Both subscription sites (hook-bridge, cli/run v2-client) use one shaper
per stream.

Tests: event-shape unit tests for started/ended/join; preemptive-compaction
integration test drives raw v2 step events through the shaper and asserts the
summarize fires (RED on the pre-fix bridge: the token cache never fills).
